# full: standard plus office, creative, virtualization and security tools
#
# Syntax: one or more packages per line, # starts a comment,
# `@include <profile>` pulls in another profile, `-pattern` removes
# packages (globs allowed) added before it.

@include standard

# All firmware instead of the curated subset
-linux-firmware-*
linux-firmware

# Every tree-sitter grammar instead of helix's vendored set
-helix-tree-sitter-vendor

